From 1a10ca2513e3ee6188cbc2e1ddfada611e06b37c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 01:29:37 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 02/19] filters: add an automatic filter that unpacks 3D video
 to full side by side

A video that signals a stereo packing (frame packing SEI, Matroska
StereoMode, MP4 stereo metadata) is converted with the stereo3d filter
to full side by side, left eye first, whatever the packing and the eye
order of the stream, and nothing is inserted for a 2D video. The
conversion can be turned off with --video-stereo=no.

The output chain tells the VO with VOCTRL_SET_STEREO_CONTENT whether
the filter is active, so that a VO can declare its video as stereo
content to the compositor. A VO that does so with its video on its own
surface sets VO_CAP_STEREO_VIEW, and the filter then gives the video the
display aspect of one view, since the window shows one view.

Assisted-by: glm-5.3:cloud (Ollama) via Codex
Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
